# Sys-datascience research records

Start with the [question map](current-question-map.md) for bounded answers and
open questions, or the [method inventory](../methods/README.md) for packets and
reproduction commands. [Current work](../../../memories/todos.md) owns assignments.

## Later review and experiments

- [September 14 review](datascience-review-2026-09-14.md) assesses the existing
  evidence and research gaps.
- [September 14 exploration wave](exploration-wave-2026-09-14.md) records the
  paired support-height, orientation-allocation, and small CEM-versus-IID results.
- [Topic maps](topics/README.md) connect earlier packets by research question;
  they predate some of the later experiments.

## Dated decision history

The July closure judgments concern their named exploration slices. They do not
settle Jörn's September assessment that data science is moderately incomplete.
Their proposed next steps and process contracts describe those sessions, not
standing assignments or restrictions on future research.

| Record | What it preserves |
| --- | --- |
| [July final account](final-research-account-2026-07-12.md) | Bounded cross-packet findings and July 15 refresh |
| [July 22 closeout](research-closeout-2026-07-22.md) | Known-seed cycle and then-current portfolio decisions |
| [Research ledger](research-ledger.md) | Decision chronology |
| [Next-session snapshot](next-session-candidates.md) and [parked lines](parked-and-rejected.md) | Historical priorities and reasons for stopping |
| [July direction review](research-direction-review-2026-07-11.md) | Closed-cycle inventory |
| [Recovery assessment](exploration-result.md) | Why the July 10 recovery closure was premature |
| [Completion contract](feature-completion-contract.md) and [portfolio contract](portfolio-review-contract.md) | Historical definitions and process decisions for that slice |

The earlier [June research ledger](../research-ledger.md) includes scratch-output
paths and exploratory observations. Retained packet artifacts, rather than those
scratch paths or copied metrics, support current numerical claims. Historical
workflow evaluations and recovery audits remain in [legacy](../legacy/README.md).
